&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;Mattermost is the leading collaborative workflow platform for defense, intelligence, security, and critical infrastructure. Trusted by the U.S. Department of War and Fortune 500s, our platform runs on-premises and in private clouds, delivering secure messaging, file sharing, workflow automation, audio/screenshare, and project management—all with full data and operational control. Mattermost powers high-stakes workflows across mission planning, real-time, real-world operations, DevSecOps, incident response, and cyber defense—enabling secure collaboration from tactical edge and DDIL environments to enterprise HQ. Teams operate across web, desktop, and mobile, with embedded interoperability for Microsoft Teams, Outlook, and Microsoft 365.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;To learn more, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.mattermost.com/&quot;&gt;www.mattermost.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Mobile Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to take ownership of the Mattermost mobile experience for teams working in defense, intelligence, and critical infrastructure. Our users operate in DDIL environments where connectivity may be disconnected, denied, intermittent, or limited, security is non-negotiable, and the software they depend on has to keep working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mobile app is primarily React Native and TypeScript today, with native iOS and Android integrations. Your immediate focus will be making that experience more reliable and performant. Over time, you&#39;ll also help shape the next generation of our cross-platform mobile architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work hands-on across application and native layers, partner closely with platform and feature teams, work directly with customer-facing teams on field reports from constrained environments, and help raise the bar for how we observe, diagnose, and build mobile software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability and Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect the app for DDIL and other constrained network environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve data and functional reliability across connection lifecycle, synchronization, recovery, and failure scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own crash-free and release-health outcomes, using telemetry to proactively identify regressions and drive them through diagnosis to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Profile and improve performance across startup, networking, storage, rendering, memory, and battery usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobile Platform Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own critical iOS and Android integrations and the boundaries between native and cross-platform code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and evolve platform capabilities including push notifications, background execution, secure storage, app lifecycle, and real-time communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build within mobile distribution and device-management constraints, including App Store, enterprise and MDM deployment, AppConfig, and Intune MAM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose production issues from native traces, telemetry, device profiling, and sparse field logs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make architecture recommendations that balance near-term delivery with the long-term direction of the mobile platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Craft and Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers on mobile architecture, reliability, performance, and platform best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold security and compliance standards required by government and enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the open-source codebase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI coding tools effectively, applying strong engineering judgment to increase output without compromising reliability or quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care about what you&#39;ve built and the problems you&#39;ve solved — not how long you&#39;ve been building. If you have strong outcomes to speak to in mobile engineering, we want to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in iOS or Android development, with strong working knowledge of the other platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of mobile architecture, platform SDKs, lifecycle constraints, and networking fundamentals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building reliable mobile systems that behave predictably through unreliable connectivity, local state changes, synchronization, and recovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mobile performance profiling and production debugging skills on real devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using production data, crash metrics, and release-health signals to drive reliability improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making architecture recommendations and owning technical outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to work across native and cross-platform codebases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI fluency and experience using coding agents to increase engineering output while applying judgment to ensure reliable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with React Native and TypeScript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile persistence, synchronization, or offline-capable systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-time communications or platform media frameworks such as WebRTC, CallKit, or Android audio APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise mobile distribution, MDM, AppConfig, or Intune MAM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building mobile software for security-sensitive, regulated, or operationally constrained environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open-source contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why Mattermost&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission-driven work:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Your contributions directly support the organizations and missions that depend on secure, reliable collaboration including the U.S. Department of War and critical infrastructure operators worldwide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first culture:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Work from anywhere with a globally distributed, high-trust team built for autonomy and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-forward environment:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We actively adopt and build AI-enabled workflows. Agentic development is core craft here, not a novelty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-end ownership:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Ship and own complex software across the full stack with real accountability for what you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open source at the core:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Be part of a vibrant developer community shaping the future of secure collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Target Salary Range: $165,000 – $215,000&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Mattermost takes a market-based approach to pay and pay may vary depending on your location. The successful candidate’s starting pay will be determined based on job-related skills, experience, qualifications, work location, and market conditions. These ranges may be modified in the future.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;Mattermost offers a remote-first work environment with medical, dental, and vision coverage. You’ll also receive unlimited PTO plus company holidays, a work from home stipend, an annual learning and development budget for conferences, certifications, and courses, paid parental leave for all parents, and a 401(k) plan.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;U.S. Eligibility &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role may require obtaining and maintaining a U.S. government security clearance. Candidates must meet federal eligibility requirements to be considered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must meet eligibility requirements for access to export-controlled information as defined by U.S. export control laws, including EAR and ITAR. For more information visit the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bis.doc.gov/&quot;&gt;Bureau of Industry and Security&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/&quot;&gt;Directorate of Defense Trade Controls&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;Mattermost is an EEO Employer, we are a remote-first, open-source company.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We are continually working to expand our hiring in more countries and regions, ensuring compliance with local laws and regulations, which takes time.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Mattermost values your unique perspective—we welcome all applicants. We encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply and are committed to assessing candidates based on their skills and qualifications. We do not tolerate discrimination against staff or applicants based on race, religion, national origin, age, disability, pregnancy status, veteran status, or other personal characteristics.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;If you require accommodations during the interview process, please let us know—we’re happy to assist.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;Mattermost is the leading collaborative workflow platform for defense, intelligence, security, and critical infrastructure. Trusted by the U.S. Department of War and Fortune 500s, our platform runs on-premises and in private clouds, delivering secure messaging, file sharing, workflow automation, audio/screenshare, and project management—all with full data and operational control. Mattermost powers high-stakes workflows across mission planning, real-time, real-world operations, DevSecOps, incident response, and cyber defense—enabling secure collaboration from tactical edge and DDIL environments to enterprise HQ. Teams operate across web, desktop, and mobile, with embedded interoperability for Microsoft Teams, Outlook, and Microsoft 365.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;To learn more, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.mattermost.com/&quot;&gt;www.mattermost.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mattermost is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Technical Account Manager (TAM)&lt;/strong&gt; to serve as a trusted technical advisor to our &lt;strong&gt;U.S. Federal and enterprise customers&lt;/strong&gt;. In this role, you will ensure the successful deployment, integration, and secure operation of the Mattermost platform in &lt;strong&gt;mission-critical and high-security environments&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will combine expertise in &lt;strong&gt;infrastructure, cybersecurity, and DevSecOps&lt;/strong&gt; with strong customer engagement and project leadership skills. As a strategic partner, you will bridge &lt;strong&gt;engineering, product, and customer teams&lt;/strong&gt;, driving secure, compliant, and scalable implementations that enable organizations to collaborate with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An active U.S. government Secret or TS/SCI clearance is a significant advantage for this position.&lt;/strong&gt; We also welcome technically strong candidates who meet the eligibility requirements to obtain a clearance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Technical Customer Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary technical advisor for strategic U.S. Federal and defense customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with technical leaders, system administrators, security teams, and executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive successful onboarding, adoption, platform optimization, and long-term customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop technical success plans aligned with customer missions, operational requirements, and business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solve Complex Technical Challenges&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide customers through deployments, upgrades, integrations, and troubleshooting across on-premises, cloud, hybrid, and air-gapped environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with Linux infrastructure, networking, containers, authentication systems, and deployment configurations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex technical issues, partnering with Engineering and Support to drive resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers improve platform reliability, security, performance, and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring a Forward-Deployed Engineering Mindset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with customers, including on-site engagements when needed, to understand and address complex operational requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer challenges into practical technical solutions, configurations, integrations, or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reusable scripts, technical playbooks, and deployment best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate independently in complex environments while collaborating closely with internal technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring field insights and customer requirements back to Product and Engineering to influence platform improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Adoption and Customer Value&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to expand Mattermost adoption across teams, workflows, and mission-critical use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct technical reviews, health assessments, and proactive optimization sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers maximize their investment through platform integrations, workflow automation, and operational best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a technical customer-facing role such as Technical Account Manager, Solutions Engineer, Customer Engineer, Technical Consultant, Support Engineer, or Forward Deployed Engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on technical experience with Linux, networking, infrastructure troubleshooting, and enterprise software deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with containers, cloud infrastructure, or modern application deployment environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to diagnose complex technical problems and collaborate across teams to deliver solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, including the ability to explain technical concepts to both engineering teams and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting enterprise, government, defense, or other complex customer environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, customer-focused mindset with a strong sense of ownership and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligibility to obtain and maintain a U.S. government security clearance, along with the ability to meet applicable U.S. export-control requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will Set You Apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Clearance and Federal Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Active Secret, Top Secret, or TS/SCI clearance — highly desirable and a significant advantage.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting DoD, Intelligence Community, federal civilian agencies, or defense contractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with secure or regulated environments, including FedRAMP, NIST 800-53, STIGs, and government security requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forward-Deployed and Technical Engineering Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly within customer environments to deploy, integrate, troubleshoot, or customize technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD pipelines, and infrastructure automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting or development experience using Python, Go, Bash, or similar languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting disconnected, degraded, intermittent, or limited-bandwidth (DDIL) environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating enterprise identity, monitoring, security, or DevSecOps systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with mobile device management technologies such as Intune or Workspace ONE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Mattermost?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission-critical impact:&lt;/strong&gt; Support organizations operating in some of the world&#39;s most demanding security environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Go beyond reactive support to influence customer architectures, deployment strategies, and platform adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct engineering collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Product and Engineering to solve meaningful technical challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt; Expand your expertise in secure infrastructure, federal technology, and forward-deployed engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Work remotely in the United States, with opportunities for direct customer engagement and on-site collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Target Salary Range:&lt;/strong&gt; $125,000 - $165,000 USD plus commission&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Mattermost takes a market-based approach to pay and pay may vary depending on your location. The successful candidate’s starting pay will be determined based on job-related skills, experience, qualifications, work location, and market conditions. These ranges may be modified in the future.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;Mattermost offers a remote-first work environment with medical, dental, and vision coverage. You’ll also receive unlimited PTO plus company holidays, a work from home stipend, an annual learning and development budget for conferences, certifications, and courses, paid parental leave for all parents, and a 401(k) plan.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
